Well, not necessarily. (Ignoring for the moment the fact that
a NH /WoF is inherently magic, and therefore something like a
wonder.)  Consider that the flash point might not be close to
the wooden tip. A conventional flammable stream of gas could,
depending on the flow velocity of the gas, inflame at some
distance from the emitting opening. Or additional emittance
of inert gas might delay contact with the necessary oxygen.
Or an additional heat-dissipating device (e.g. a metallic net)
could allow the gas to be inflamed only beyond that device.

But okay, that's all physical options, and Nethack wands work
differently, I'm sure.

